WEBVTT

00:05.040 --> 00:07.770
Yeah, shall we go somewhere together?

00:07.770 --> 00:09.720
Sure, I'd love to!

00:09.720 --> 00:11.480
Where though?

00:11.480 --> 00:12.650
Wherever you like.

00:12.650 --> 00:14.760
I'll let you decide.

00:14.760 --> 00:15.870
Then...

00:15.870 --> 00:17.880
I'd love to visit the castle town!

00:17.880 --> 00:19.350
I want to do some shopping,

00:19.350 --> 00:22.500
and it'd be nice to be able to take
my time and enjoy the scenery.

00:22.500 --> 00:23.950
Okay, it's decided then.

00:23.950 --> 00:25.520
I can't wait!

00:25.520 --> 00:27.710
It'll be so wonderful there with all our friends!

00:28.080 --> 00:29.980
Well, I was thinking...

00:32.840 --> 00:34.300
Maybe it could be just the two of us.

00:37.490 --> 00:38.680
Okay!

00:39.410 --> 00:42.680
<i>One simple promise gives me hope.</i>

00:45.850 --> 00:48.650
<i>And so I can keep going forward without hesitation.</i>

00:49.590 --> 00:51.160
<i>Keep walking this path...</i>

00:52.980 --> 00:54.910
<i>And make my story move towards the horizon.</i>

01:02.680 --> 01:03.950
Amazing.

01:04.450 --> 01:07.350
You did all this by yourself, Shirayuki?

01:07.350 --> 01:08.000
I did!

01:08.000 --> 01:11.380
The Chief Herbalist's desk is perfectly clean.

01:11.380 --> 01:12.550
How many times a year...

01:12.550 --> 01:15.430
No, how many times in my <i>life</i> have I seen that?

01:18.640 --> 01:21.020
I just cleaned everything at once.

01:21.020 --> 01:25.720
I wanted to take the day off tomorrow,
so I tried to get ahead on tomorrow's work.

01:25.720 --> 01:27.970
Ah, right, you asked me about that.

01:27.970 --> 01:29.690
Got any big plans for tomorrow?

01:29.690 --> 01:30.760
Yes!

01:30.760 --> 01:32.900
I'm going shopping in the town.

01:32.900 --> 01:34.020
I see.

01:34.020 --> 01:36.990
It'll be your first day off in a while,
so have fun with it!

01:37.480 --> 01:38.310
I will!

01:39.250 --> 01:40.490
I'll be leaving now.

01:44.480 --> 01:47.080
Something tells me she's planning
to do more than shop.

01:47.710 --> 01:49.320
You can tell?

01:49.320 --> 01:52.340
That coy smile, the pitter-patter of excited steps...

01:53.060 --> 01:55.960
It's as plain as day in my eyes.

01:57.170 --> 02:00.140
She's going there to play around!

02:01.180 --> 02:02.190
Did you know?

02:02.190 --> 02:03.980
There's a new shop in the town.

02:03.980 --> 02:09.400
They have all these fluffy puppies to play
with while you drink delicious tea!

02:09.400 --> 02:11.510
Shirayuki's clearly done her homework.

02:11.510 --> 02:14.160
She knows what's popular!

02:14.160 --> 02:15.160
I see!

02:15.160 --> 02:16.780
You're sharp, Chief Herbalist!

02:18.150 --> 02:20.130
Somehow, I don't think that's it.

03:51.040 --> 03:55.330
The Trivial Treasures

03:53.400 --> 03:56.250
Like I said, I'm going to the town with Shirayuki.

03:56.730 --> 03:57.930
Just the two of you?

03:57.930 --> 03:58.710
Yeah.

03:59.100 --> 04:02.960
After the Yuris Island affair,
we haven't had any free time,

04:02.960 --> 04:05.300
but it looks like we finally have some time
to breathe, so I decided to go out.

04:05.630 --> 04:10.480
You <i>have</i> been weirdly focused on your work lately.

04:10.480 --> 04:12.700
I'll be gone for the whole day, won't I?

04:13.860 --> 04:15.810
Can Kiki and I tag along?

04:17.920 --> 04:19.570
I'm kidding, I swear.

04:19.570 --> 04:22.450
Well, I guess it <i>is</i> a date after all.

04:24.120 --> 04:26.460
You know, Missy mentioned it to me as well.

04:26.460 --> 04:30.070
She only said that she's going
out with you to the town,

04:30.070 --> 04:32.040
but to think it was actually a date...

04:32.380 --> 04:35.370
I wish you wouldn't assume things like that!

04:35.370 --> 04:38.240
You know, it's because you're so stiff

04:38.240 --> 04:42.840
that you still haven't told Missy that
she's cute or something nice like that.

04:44.100 --> 04:46.210
As if you would know anything about that!

04:46.210 --> 04:48.750
Oh, it seems I've struck a nerve!

04:48.750 --> 04:50.430
I thought as much.

04:51.600 --> 04:54.250
How about telling her something nice once in a while?

04:55.960 --> 04:59.590
Like "Oh, you look nice today!" or something.

04:59.590 --> 05:02.390
I bet you're thinking that, just not saying out loud.

05:02.390 --> 05:03.150
I have, actually.

05:03.780 --> 05:05.670
In fact, I did tell her something
looked nice on her once.

05:05.670 --> 05:07.870
Oh? When was that?

05:08.960 --> 05:11.290
On Castle Visitation Day.

05:11.960 --> 05:14.660
About the hair ornament you gave her.

05:16.710 --> 05:18.920
Do you want to get thrown out?

05:19.340 --> 05:21.110
Show me how it's done, then!

05:21.690 --> 05:22.990
First, Mitsuhide!

05:23.800 --> 05:25.570
Don't bring me into this!

05:25.570 --> 05:28.010
But look, my young noble, it's your chance to shine!

05:28.010 --> 05:30.140
Imagine Missy is there!

05:30.430 --> 05:31.760
Here! Seduce her!

05:38.540 --> 05:41.610
Shirayuki, you're always
so composed, it's quite cute!

05:46.490 --> 05:49.620
Hey! I thought we were all working together here!

05:53.170 --> 05:54.730
Please, continue.

05:54.730 --> 05:55.800
Well, you see...

05:55.800 --> 05:58.500
My apologies if we were being too loud.

06:10.180 --> 06:11.680
Now I'm ready!

06:14.300 --> 06:15.500
Missy.

06:15.500 --> 06:16.980
Have you finished preparing?

06:16.980 --> 06:18.260
Obi!

06:18.260 --> 06:21.150
I'll take you to meet him.

06:22.700 --> 06:24.150
I'm leaving the rest in your hands.

06:24.150 --> 06:25.250
Okay.

06:25.250 --> 06:26.900
Take care, Zen.

06:32.080 --> 06:33.530
Hey, Mitsuhide.

06:33.850 --> 06:35.010
Yes?

06:35.010 --> 06:36.370
What's a date?

06:37.620 --> 06:39.690
I heard the soldiers talking about it.

06:39.690 --> 06:41.120
So what's a date?

06:42.000 --> 06:44.430
U-Um... How to put it...

06:44.430 --> 06:49.610
It's when you go out somewhere
with your significant other, I guess.

06:49.610 --> 06:52.470
You walk around the town, shop together...

06:52.470 --> 06:53.950
Is that all?

06:53.950 --> 06:56.850
You eat together, hold hands...

06:56.850 --> 06:58.000
Oh!

06:58.000 --> 07:00.170
I see. And then kiss, right?

07:00.170 --> 07:02.230
You'd probably be too stiff to try!

07:07.860 --> 07:10.030
But it's also not something I'll ever get to do.

07:10.810 --> 07:13.130
No wonder I've never heard about it.

07:17.790 --> 07:19.460
You never know.

07:20.110 --> 07:22.710
Maybe someday a day will come when you will.

07:25.690 --> 07:27.170
Keep dreaming.

07:27.670 --> 07:29.290
Time sure flies, huh?

07:29.890 --> 07:31.070
What's wrong?

07:31.070 --> 07:33.760
Nothing, just lost in a memory.

07:35.800 --> 07:37.260
The weather sure is nice today.

07:37.760 --> 07:38.810
Agreed.

07:43.710 --> 07:46.020
Master should come soon, right?

07:46.410 --> 07:48.600
Y-Yeah.

07:48.600 --> 07:51.450
Missy, don't tell me you're nervous!

07:51.450 --> 07:53.670
Why would I be?!

07:53.670 --> 07:55.380
You don't seem like yourself today.

07:55.380 --> 07:57.380
You're tense.

07:57.380 --> 07:59.120
R-Really?

07:59.990 --> 08:04.870
A day out with Zen should feel normal.
I've never really thought about it before.

08:05.430 --> 08:07.090
But I just can't calm down today.

08:07.090 --> 08:09.510
If that's the case, perhaps I should come along.

08:10.960 --> 08:12.260
I'm just joking!

08:12.260 --> 08:15.170
I have to say though,
I didn't expect us to run into Ryu!

08:15.170 --> 08:17.620
I came here to buy a book on herbs.

08:17.620 --> 08:23.080
And Chief Herbalist told me to find out
where Shirayuki was going today.

08:23.940 --> 08:26.770
Don't worry. It's none of my business.

08:27.180 --> 08:28.730
Thanks.

08:29.290 --> 08:31.760
There's the Missy I'm used to seeing.

08:31.760 --> 08:32.750
Really?

08:32.750 --> 08:37.980
Yeah, just relax and act like you always do.

08:37.980 --> 08:40.150
I will. Thanks, Obi.

08:41.260 --> 08:43.780
Missy, I see a certain Master is here.

08:43.780 --> 08:45.990
Look, up there!

08:50.910 --> 08:52.760
Looks like you're having fun.

08:53.240 --> 08:54.630
I didn't know Ryu would come too.

08:54.630 --> 08:56.950
I'm going back to the castle now.

08:56.950 --> 08:59.470
I'm only here to accompany Missy.

08:59.470 --> 09:00.100
I'll head back too.

09:00.580 --> 09:01.900
See you at the castle!

09:01.900 --> 09:03.060
See you there!

09:07.190 --> 09:08.120
Shall we go?

09:08.120 --> 09:09.150
Of course! After you!

09:13.960 --> 09:14.850
What's that?

09:14.850 --> 09:16.360
Did you already buy something?

09:16.700 --> 09:18.260
That's our lunch.

09:18.260 --> 09:20.860
Didn't I say I'd bring it?

09:20.860 --> 09:22.030
Oh, right.

09:22.030 --> 09:23.260
When should we eat?

09:23.260 --> 09:26.370
Let's walk around the town for a bit first.

09:27.550 --> 09:29.000
It sure is lively here.

09:29.000 --> 09:31.690
Yeah. I've been to town many times,

09:31.690 --> 09:34.280
but I never walk around or go into the shops.

09:34.280 --> 09:36.380
It seems easy to get lost here.

09:36.380 --> 09:40.890
I also come to the pharmacy here quite often.

09:41.620 --> 09:43.560
What a lovely smell!

09:45.060 --> 09:47.200
They look so tasty.

09:47.200 --> 09:50.030
Maybe we can buy some to take home to everyone?

09:50.030 --> 09:52.000
A present for them, huh?

09:52.000 --> 09:57.030
We always go out together,
so I never buy anything for them.

09:57.030 --> 09:59.990
Do Kiki and Mitsuhide like sweets?

09:59.990 --> 10:04.240
Mitsuhide likes everything sweet, yeah.

10:04.240 --> 10:08.010
I've never seen Kiki eating sweets though.

10:08.010 --> 10:11.170
They both seem so different!

10:11.540 --> 10:15.590
Yeah, but they've been friends for so long,
it's like they share the same heartbeat.

10:16.300 --> 10:20.450
Ever since that first meeting, I was positive
they'd work well together with me.

10:23.890 --> 10:25.840
Ah, Miss Kiki.

10:25.840 --> 10:28.340
Good morning, Sir Mitsuhide.

10:28.340 --> 10:30.700
Huh? Where is Prince Zen?

10:30.700 --> 10:33.300
He... is here, theoretically.

10:36.760 --> 10:38.200
Prince Zen!

10:38.200 --> 10:40.360
Oh, it's just you, Mitsuhide.

10:40.360 --> 10:44.330
You can't sleep on the floor, Prince Zen!

10:44.700 --> 10:48.810
I was exhausted after finishing
yesterday's inspections. What can I say?

10:48.810 --> 10:50.790
Good morning, Your Highness.

10:52.010 --> 10:54.800
Should I wake you if this happens in the future?

10:54.800 --> 10:57.340
It'd be better if you didn't have to at all.

10:57.340 --> 10:59.260
But if it does happen again, please wake him.

10:59.260 --> 11:00.890
Understood.

11:00.890 --> 11:04.720
Your Highness, I'd like to confirm today's plans.

11:04.720 --> 11:07.290
Actually, I have something to ask you, Kiki.

11:07.290 --> 11:07.850
Yes?

11:08.220 --> 11:13.030
I don't really like treating the people
around me like servants.

11:13.570 --> 11:17.940
If you don't mind, it'd be nice if we could
just talk casually when it's just us three.

11:19.240 --> 11:21.660
Also, Mitsuhide...

11:21.660 --> 11:26.660
Ever since Kiki came along,
you've reverted back to your old ways!

11:26.660 --> 11:28.190
I thought we'd been over this.

11:28.190 --> 11:30.040
Z-Zen...

11:30.390 --> 11:34.000
If Your Highness wishes it, I'll do my best.

11:34.000 --> 11:35.840
Great. Call me Zen.

11:36.190 --> 11:37.460
Okay, Zen.

11:38.460 --> 11:40.220
She's so quick to adapt!

11:49.430 --> 11:51.230
Here, Miss Kiki.

11:52.020 --> 11:53.140
Thank you.

11:54.430 --> 11:55.430
Excuse me.

11:55.980 --> 11:57.720
I wonder if I shouldn't have done that.

11:57.720 --> 11:58.920
Sir Mitsuhide.

11:59.440 --> 12:00.360
Yes?

12:00.360 --> 12:02.240
It's about language, but...

12:02.240 --> 12:04.960
Could you call me Kiki?

12:05.870 --> 12:08.640
When I'm being called Miss Kiki,

12:08.640 --> 12:11.750
it's difficult calling His Highness just Zen.

12:11.750 --> 12:13.410
I see.

12:13.410 --> 12:15.150
I can understand that.

12:15.150 --> 12:18.340
You can call me Mitsuhide too, then.

12:18.340 --> 12:20.160
Am I really allowed?

12:20.160 --> 12:22.090
Yes, I don't mind.

12:22.090 --> 12:24.340
Understood, Mitsuhide.

12:25.460 --> 12:26.190
Well then.

12:27.770 --> 12:28.810
Miss Kiki!

12:32.270 --> 12:33.270
No...

12:35.030 --> 12:37.060
Ki... Kiki.

12:44.330 --> 12:45.660
Zen!

12:46.490 --> 12:48.330
Looks like you two sure are getting along!

12:50.290 --> 12:53.710
They haven't changed at all since then.

12:55.080 --> 12:56.260
<i>You haven't either.</i>

12:57.260 --> 13:03.050
Surely we can talk about something other
than Mitsuhide while we're alone though.

13:03.050 --> 13:04.170
Okay!

13:04.170 --> 13:07.130
No more talking about Mitsuhide starting right now.

13:07.650 --> 13:09.280
Not until we get back home.

13:11.110 --> 13:12.430
Shall we walk a bit more?

13:13.390 --> 13:14.440
Of course!

13:18.300 --> 13:19.440
I've returned!

13:19.810 --> 13:20.940
How was it?

13:20.940 --> 13:23.120
No need to worry.

13:23.120 --> 13:26.260
I made sure Missy got to town safely.

13:26.260 --> 13:29.590
They're having plenty of fun together right now.

13:29.590 --> 13:30.410
I see.

13:30.410 --> 13:32.580
Since we don't get days off often,

13:32.580 --> 13:36.330
shouldn't you go on a date with Miss Kiki too?

13:36.330 --> 13:37.980
On a date with Kiki?

13:40.610 --> 13:42.680
A date with Kiki, huh?

13:42.680 --> 13:44.440
That might actually be nice.

13:46.840 --> 13:48.010
Oh, Miss Kiki!

13:50.940 --> 13:52.130
She locked the door!

13:52.130 --> 13:55.210
We got locked in here, Mitsuhide!

13:55.210 --> 13:58.300
<i>She doesn't want it </i>that<i> much?!</i>

14:00.470 --> 14:01.980
What do you want to see next?

14:01.980 --> 14:04.690
Didn't you want to do some shopping?

14:04.690 --> 14:07.690
Right! I wanted some stationary for writing letters!

14:08.250 --> 14:09.490
Letters?

14:10.740 --> 14:12.740
They have so many different ones.

14:15.700 --> 14:18.120
It says that's a fragrant sealing wax!

14:18.120 --> 14:19.140
Let's see.

14:21.410 --> 14:22.720
It's really nice.

14:25.290 --> 14:26.420
It really is!

14:27.740 --> 14:29.840
I'll take it, then.

14:29.840 --> 14:35.450
I should write to the people in Laxdo,
like Shuka, and to people from Tanbarun.

14:35.450 --> 14:36.600
You're so diligent.

14:36.970 --> 14:39.650
There are many people I don't
have time to go see, after all.

14:39.650 --> 14:42.150
That's why we sometimes exchange letters.

14:42.810 --> 14:45.070
I wouldn't think you would, but...

14:45.630 --> 14:48.450
You're not getting any letters from Raj, are you?

14:49.090 --> 14:50.630
Prince Raj?

14:50.630 --> 14:52.910
No, no, of course not!

14:55.480 --> 14:57.340
Wh-What is this?

14:57.340 --> 14:59.920
Cake, filled to the brim with apples, my prince.

14:59.920 --> 15:01.540
I can see that much!

15:01.540 --> 15:03.640
What's the meaning of this, Sakaki?!

15:03.640 --> 15:06.400
I told you not to feed me apples!

15:06.400 --> 15:09.800
Perhaps the kitchen staff
had an abundance of apples.

15:09.800 --> 15:11.930
I promise it wasn't meant to be malicious.

15:12.610 --> 15:15.100
Please, have some more apple tea.

15:15.100 --> 15:17.350
<i>Apples remind me of her too much.</i>

15:17.350 --> 15:18.850
<i>The apple-haired girl.</i>

15:21.900 --> 15:25.520
Actually, it's been a while since
the last time you held a ball.

15:26.150 --> 15:28.370
Has something changed?

15:28.370 --> 15:30.670
It's not because of any particular reason.

15:30.670 --> 15:32.240
They bore me is all.

15:32.240 --> 15:33.800
I see.

15:34.770 --> 15:36.810
<i>Boredom makes me remember...</i>

15:35.810 --> 15:37.240
Those times.

15:36.810 --> 15:37.620
Those times.

15:40.090 --> 15:41.730
I'm not doing this anymore!

15:41.730 --> 15:43.540
It's a waste of time! That's boring!

15:43.540 --> 15:45.600
Crying over some blisters...

15:45.600 --> 15:48.010
We haven't even been doing this for three days.

15:48.010 --> 15:50.880
Won't it be fine if you just protect me yourself?

15:53.750 --> 15:58.850
Prince Raj, who was raised as the
spoiled first prince of his kingdom,

15:58.850 --> 16:03.410
already had it in his mind that he'd
get everything he wanted from me.

16:04.480 --> 16:06.590
Prince Raj, it's time for your politics studies.

16:06.590 --> 16:08.030
My stomach hurts!

16:08.710 --> 16:11.020
Prince Raj, it's time for your horse riding lessons.

16:11.020 --> 16:13.530
I don't need more lessons!

16:14.550 --> 16:17.770
Whatever he did, he'd grow bored quickly,

16:17.770 --> 16:19.870
and yet, there was one thing he enjoyed.

16:21.370 --> 16:23.930
Prince Raj excelled in the fine arts.

16:25.000 --> 16:29.180
He found a home in poetry where
he could express himself gracefully.

16:30.860 --> 16:33.260
This makes me remember the old days, Prince Raj.

16:33.630 --> 16:34.480
What makes you?

16:34.480 --> 16:36.060
Ah, nothing.

16:36.060 --> 16:39.240
I was just remembering you used to be
quite skilled at composing poems.

16:39.240 --> 16:43.730
How about sending Miss Shirayuki
a poem about her?

16:44.050 --> 16:46.230
A poem about Miss Shirayuki?

16:52.850 --> 16:56.850
R-Red... red flower you are,

16:56.850 --> 16:58.490
but a flower with thorns you are.

16:58.490 --> 16:59.840
You've lost your skill, I suppose.

17:01.260 --> 17:03.710
Did you bake this, Shirayuki?

17:03.710 --> 17:04.960
Yeah!

17:04.960 --> 17:09.130
Kiki told me you like pies,
so I thought I'd make one for you.

17:09.130 --> 17:10.460
Here, take a piece.

17:13.260 --> 17:14.170
It's great!

17:14.500 --> 17:15.860
That's good to hear.

17:18.420 --> 17:21.740
Shirayuki, did you see something
today that you wanted?

17:22.770 --> 17:24.560
I'd like to buy it for you.

17:25.590 --> 17:27.560
F-For me?

17:27.560 --> 17:28.250
Yeah.

17:28.250 --> 17:29.480
You don't have to!

17:30.480 --> 17:32.400
Then it's decided. I'll give you a memento.

17:34.400 --> 17:35.680
Something to remember today by.

17:35.680 --> 17:36.620
What do you want?

17:36.620 --> 17:37.460
A dress?

17:37.460 --> 17:40.600
I-I don't really know much about dresses...

17:43.710 --> 17:46.110
They apparently have a lot of things here.

17:46.110 --> 17:47.850
Pens, ornaments, and so on.

17:47.850 --> 17:48.890
They really do.

17:48.890 --> 17:50.290
So many things here!

17:51.490 --> 17:52.530
Shirayuki!

17:57.300 --> 17:58.850
Bookmarks!

17:58.850 --> 18:00.380
So pretty...

18:06.680 --> 18:08.500
Do you like this one?

18:08.500 --> 18:10.010
Ah, yeah.

18:14.650 --> 18:17.320
Th-Thank you.

18:18.230 --> 18:20.070
Thank you, Zen.

18:34.140 --> 18:37.940
I heard once that you're supposed
to do this on such a lovely day.

18:37.940 --> 18:39.400
Who said that?

18:39.400 --> 18:41.260
Who was it, I wonder...

18:41.260 --> 18:43.780
I feel like his name started with M.

18:45.150 --> 18:48.490
<i>We took each other's hand and began our story.</i>

18:49.550 --> 18:53.860
<i>I hope the sound of its pages being turned</i>

18:53.860 --> 18:57.060
<i>will, like our footsteps, echo in unison</i>

18:57.060 --> 18:58.600
<i>as we continue walking together.</i>

19:20.150 --> 19:22.180
We've walked so much!

19:22.180 --> 19:24.630
Do your feet hurt?

19:24.630 --> 19:26.680
No, I'm fine.

19:27.520 --> 19:31.230
Zen, is there anything else you wanted to look at?

19:31.230 --> 19:32.380
Anything else?

19:32.380 --> 19:33.430
Yes.

19:33.430 --> 19:36.690
Like your own souvenir or memento.

19:37.070 --> 19:40.900
If there's anything <i>you</i> want, I want to know that.

19:42.000 --> 19:43.070
Is this for a gift to me?

19:43.390 --> 19:44.360
Exactly!

20:01.780 --> 20:04.640
I'm not sure. I...

20:20.870 --> 20:23.530
Shirayuki, did you have fun today?

20:24.790 --> 20:25.970
So much fun!

20:27.200 --> 20:30.630
Those words are the greatest present for me.

20:39.840 --> 20:40.950
Mitsuhide!

20:41.450 --> 20:42.350
Kiki!

20:43.260 --> 20:44.710
Obi.

20:44.710 --> 20:46.170
Don't sleep in a place like that.

20:47.680 --> 20:49.350
You're giving these to us?

20:49.350 --> 20:50.340
Are these presents?

20:50.340 --> 20:52.430
Yeah, and I'm going to sleep now.

20:53.640 --> 20:55.560
I'll be counting on you tomorrow again.

21:09.330 --> 21:11.200
Is that for me?

21:11.530 --> 21:12.900
When did you write it?

21:13.490 --> 21:16.240
While you were getting the bookmark wrapped,

21:16.240 --> 21:18.460
I found somewhere to write a letter.

21:19.110 --> 21:23.460
A letter with only two lines.
Just what I'd expect from Shirayuki.

21:26.020 --> 21:27.340
It has a really nice fragrance.

21:28.800 --> 21:29.970
<i>Dear Zen,</i>

21:30.600 --> 21:33.810
<i>I'm happy we got to walk around town together.</i>

21:34.420 --> 21:37.890
<i>Thank you for today.</i>

21:41.560 --> 21:42.780
What's that?

21:42.780 --> 21:45.610
An ink bottle that glows at night, apparently.

21:45.970 --> 21:48.490
Mine appears to be a brooch with a dog on it.

21:48.490 --> 21:49.540
That's a cat.

21:49.540 --> 21:52.050
No, that's obviously a lion.

21:52.050 --> 21:53.200
What did you get?

21:53.200 --> 21:56.960
An antique ornamental cork for liquor bottles, apparently.

21:59.410 --> 22:03.910
I suppose it <i>is</i> the first time Zen's
bought presents for anyone, isn't it?

22:03.910 --> 22:07.140
I just want to know if he put
any thought into these gifts.

22:07.140 --> 22:09.760
I really wonder where I should put mine.

22:09.760 --> 22:11.970
How about hanging it on your neck like a pendant?

22:11.970 --> 22:12.700
Lame...

22:12.700 --> 22:13.650
Don't say that!

22:13.650 --> 22:15.000
Don't finish that thought!

22:15.000 --> 22:16.380
I'll definitely use mine!

22:16.380 --> 22:19.430
It's cool how it shines at night!

22:19.430 --> 22:20.530
Look!

22:20.530 --> 22:22.540
It shines like a rainbow!

22:22.540 --> 22:23.290
Yeah.

22:23.290 --> 22:24.670
Dazzling.
